040289,000542:                                                                                          	# THE ELEMENTS OF THE NAV BASE MATRIX WHICH WE MUST DIVIDE BY COS(MGA)
040290,000543:                                                                                          	# ALREADY CONTAIN COS(MGA)/2 AS A FACTOR. THEREFORE THE QUOTIENT SHOULD
040291,000544:                                                                                          	# ORDINARILY NEVER EXCEED 1/2 IN MAGNITUDE.  BUT IF THE MGA IS NEAR PI/2
040292,000545:                                                                                          	# THEN COS(MGA) IS NEAR ZERO, AND THERE MAY BE SOME CHAFF IN THE OTHER
040293,000546:                                                                                          	# ELEMENTS OF THE MATRIX WHICH WOULD PRODUCE CHAOS UNDER DIVISION.
040294,000547:                                                                                          	# BEFORE DIVIDING WE MAKE SURE COS(MGA) IS AT LEAST ONE BIT LARGER
040295,000548:                                                                                          	# THAN THE MAGNITUDE OF THE HIGH ORDER PART OF THE OPERAND.
040296,000549: 
040297,000550:                                                                                          	# IF ONE OR MORE DIVIDES CANNOT BE PERFORMED, THIS MEANS THAT THE
040298,000551:                                                                                          	# REQUIRED MGA IS VERY NEARLY +-PI/2 AND THEREFORE THE OTHER GIMBAL
040299,000552:                                                                                          	# ANGLES ARE INDETERMINATE.  THE INNER AND OUTER GIMBAL ANGLES RETURNED
040300,000553:                                                                                          	# IN THIS CASE WILL BE RANDOM MULTIPLES OF PI/2.
