051380,000023:                                                                                          	## This source code has been transcribed or otherwise adapted from
051381,000024:                                                                                          	## digitized images of a hardcopy from the MIT Museum.  The digitization
051382,000025:                                                                                          	## was performed by Paul Fjeld, and arranged for by Deborah Douglas of
051383,000026:                                                                                          	## the Museum.  Many thanks to both.  The images (with suitable reduction
051384,000027:                                                                                          	## in storage size and consequent reduction in image quality as well) are
051385,000028:                                                                                          	## available online at www.ibiblio.org/apollo.  If for some reason you
051386,000029:                                                                                          	## find that the images are illegible, contact me at info@sandroid.org
051387,000030:                                                                                          	## about getting access to the (much) higher-quality images which Paul
051388,000031:                                                                                          	## actually created.
051389,000032:                                                                                          	##
051390,000033:                                                                                          	## Notations on the hardcopy document read, in part:
051391,000034:                                                                                          	##
051392,000035:                                                                                          	##      Assemble revision 001 of AGC program LMY99 by NASA 2021112-61
051393,000036:                                                                                          	##      16:27 JULY 14, 1969 
051394,000037: 
051396,000039:                                                                                          	# 1.0 INTRODUCTION
051397,000040:                                                                                          	# ----------------
051398,000041: 
051399,000042:                                                                                          	# FROM A USERS POINT OF VIEW, ORBITAL INTEGRATION IS ESSENTIALLY THE SAME AS THE 278 INTEGRATION
051400,000043:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM.  THE SAME ENTRANCES TO THE PROGRAM WILL BE MAINTAINED, THE SAME STALLING ROUTINE WILL BE USED AND
051401,000044:                                                                                          	# OUTPUT WILL STILL BE VIA THE PUSHLIST.  THE PRIMARY DIFFERENCES TO A USER INVOLVE THE ADDED CAPABILITY OF
051402,000045:                                                                                          	# TERMINATING INTEGRATION AT A SPECIFIC FINAL RADIUS AND THE DIFFERENCE IN STATE VECTOR SCALING INSIDE AND OUT-
051403,000046:                                                                                          	# SIDE THE LUNAR SPHERE OF INFLUENCE.
051404,000047: 
051405,000048:                                                                                          	# IN ORDER TO MAKE THE CSM(LEM)PREC AND CSM(LEM)CONIC ENTRANCES SIMILAR TO FLIGHT 278, THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM
051406,000049:                                                                                          	# WILL ITSELF SET THE FINAL RADIUS (RFINAL) TO 0 SO THAT REACHING THE DESIRED TIME ONLY WILL TERMINATE
051407,000050:                                                                                          	# INTEGRATION.  THE DP REGISTER RFINAL MUST BE SET BY USERS OF INTEGRVS AND INTEGRV, AND MUST BE DONE AFTER THE
051408,000051:                                                                                          	# CALL TC INTSTALL.
051409,000052: 
051410,000053:                                                                                          	# WHEN THE LM IS ON THE LUNAR SURFACE (INDICATED BY LUNAR SURFACE FLAG SET) CALLS TO LEMCONIC, LEMPREC, AND
051411,000054:                                                                                          	# INTEGRV WITH VINFLAG = 0 WILL RESULT IN THE USE OF THE PLANETARY INERTIAL ORIENTATION SUBROUTINES TO PROVIDE
051412,000055:                                                                                          	# BOTH THE LMS POSITION AND VELOCITY IN THE REFERENCE COORDINATE SYSTEM.
051413,000056:                                                                                          	# THE PROGRAM WILL PROVIDE OUTPUT AS IF INTEGRATION WAS USED.  THAT IS, THE PUSHLIST WILL BE SET AS NOTED BELOW AND
051414,000057:                                                                                          	# THE PERMANENT STATE VECTOR UPDATED WHEN SPECIFIED BY AN INTEGRV CALL.
051415,000058: 
051416,000059:                                                                                          	# USERS OF INTEGRVS DESIRING INTEGRATION (INTYPFLG = 0) SHOULD NOTE THAT THE OBLATENESS PERTURBATION COMPUTATION
051417,000060:                                                                                          	# IN LUNAR ORBIT IS TIME DEPENDENT.  THEREFORE, THE USER SHOULD SUPPLY AN INITIAL STATE VECTOR VALID AT SOME REAL
051418,000061:                                                                                          	# TIME AND THE DESIRED TIME (TDEC1) ALSO AT SOME REAL TIME.  FOR CONIC ,,INTEGRATION,, THE USER MAY STILL USE ZERO
051419,000062:                                                                                          	# AS THE INITIAL TIME AND DELTA TIME AS THE DESIRED TIME.
051420,000063: 
051421,000064:                                                                                          	# 2.0 GENERAL DESCRIPTION
051422,000065:                                                                                          	# -----------------------
051423,000066: 
051424,000067:                                                                                          	# THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM OPERATES AS A CLOSED INTERPRETIVE SUBROUTINE AND PERFORMS THESE FUNCTIONS ---
051425,000068:                                                                                          	#       1) INTEGRATES (PRECISION OR CONIC) EITHER CSM OR LM STATE VECTOR
051426,000069:                                                                                          	#       2) INTEGRATES THE W-MATRIX
051427,000070:                                                                                          	#       3) PERMANENT OR TEMPORARY UPDATE OF THE STATE VECTOR
051428,000071: 
051429,000072:                                                                                          	# THERE ARE SIX ENTRANCES TO THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM.  FOUR OF THESE (CSMPREC, LEMPREC, CSMCONIC, LEMCONIC) SET
051430,000073:                                                                                          	# ALL THE FLAGS REQUIRED IN THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM ITSELF TO CAUSE THE PRECISION OR CONIC INTEGRATION (KEPLER) OF
051431,000074:                                                                                          	# THE LM OR CSM STATE VECTOR, AS THE NAMES SUGGEST.  ONE ENTRANCE (INTEGRVS) PERMITS THE CALLING PROGRAM TO
051432,000075:                                                                                          	# PROVIDE A STATE VECTOR TO BE INTEGRATED.  THE CALLING PROGRAM MUST SET THE FLAGS INDICATING (1) PRECISION OR
051433,000076:                                                                                          	# CONIC INTEGRATION, (2) IN OR OUT OF LUNAR SPHERE, (3) MIDCOURSE OR NOT, AND THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM COMPLETES
051434,000077:                                                                                          	# THE FLAG SETTING TO BYPASS W-MATRIX INTEGRATION.  THE LAST ENTRANCE (INTEGRV, USED IN GENERAL BY THE
051435,000078:                                                                                          	# NAVIGATION PROGRAMS) PERMITS THE CALLER TO SET FIVE FLAGS (NOT MOONFLAG OR MIDFLAG) BUT NOT TO INPUT A STATE
051436,000079:                                                                                          	# VECTOR.  ANY PROGRAM WHICH CALLS INTEGRVS OR INTEGRV MUST CALL INTSTALL BEFORE IT SETS THE INTEGRATION FLAGS
051437,000080:                                                                                          	# AND/OR STATE VECTOR.
051438,000081: 
051439,000082:                                                                                          	# THREE SETS OF 42 REGISTERS AND 2 FLAGS ARE USED FOR THE STATE VECTORS.  TWO SETS, WHICH MAY NOT BE OVERLAYED, ARE
051440,000083:                                                                                          	# USED FOR THE PERMANENT STATE VECTORS FOR THE CSM AND LM.  THE THIRD SET, WHICH MAY BE OVERLAYED WHEN INTEGRATION
051441,000084:                                                                                          	# IS NOT BEING DONE, IS USED IN THE COMPUTATIONS.
051442,000085: 
051443,000086:                                                                                          	# THE PERMANENT STATE VECTORS WILL BE PERIODICALLY UPDATED SO THAT THE VECTORS WILL NOT BE OLDER THAN 4 TIMESTEPS.
051444,000087:                                                                                          	# THE PERMANENT STATE VECTORS WILL ALSO BE UPDATED WHENEVER THE W-MATRIX IS INTEGRATED OR WHEN A CALLER OF INTEGRV
051445,000088:                                                                                          	# SETS STATEFLG (THE NAVIGATION PROGRAMS P20, P22.)
051446,000089: 
051448,000091:                                                                                          	# APPENDIX B OF THE USERS GUIDE LISTS THE STATE VECTOR QUANTITIES.
051449,000092: 
051450,000093:                                                                                          	# 2.1 RESTARTS
051451,000094: 
051452,000095:                                                                                          	# PHASE CHANGES WILL BE MADE IN THE INTEGRATION PROGRAM ONLY FOR THE INTEGRV ENTRANCE (I.E., WHEN THE W-MATRIX IS
051453,000096:                                                                                          	# INTEGRATED OR PERMANENT STATE VECTOR IS UPDATED.)  THE GROUP NUMBER USED WILL BE THAT FOR THE P20-25 PROGRAMS
051454,000097:                                                                                          	# (I.E., GROUP2) SINCE THE INTEGRV ENTRANCE WILL ONLY BE USED BY THESE PROGRAMS.  IF A RESTART OCCURS DURING AN
051455,000098:                                                                                          	# INTEGRATION OF THE STATE VECTOR ONLY, THE RECOVERY WILL BE TO THE LAST PHASE IN THE CALLING PROGRAM.  CALLING
051456,000099:                                                                                          	# PROGRAMS WHICH USE THE INTEGRV OR INTEGRVS ENTRANCE OF INTEGRATION SHOULD ENSURE THAT IF PHASE CHANGING IS DONE
051457,000100:                                                                                          	# THAT IT IS PRIOR TO SETTING THE INTEGRATION INPUTS IN THE PUSHLIST.
051458,000101:                                                                                          	# THIS IS BECAUSE THE PUSHLIST IS LOST DURING A RESTART.
051459,000102: 
051460,000103:                                                                                          	# 2.2 SCALING
051461,000104: 
051462,000105:                                                                                          	# THE INTEGRATION ROUTINE WILL MAINTAIN THE PERMANENT MEMORY STATE VECTORS IN THE SCALING AND UNITS DEFINED IN
051463,000106:                                                                                          	# APPENDIX B OF THE USERS GUIDE.  THE SCALING OF THE OUTPUT POSITION VECTOR DEPENDS ON THE ORIGIN OF THE COORDINATE
051464,000107:                                                                                          	# SYSTEM AT THE DESIRED INTEGRATION TIME.  THE COORDINATE SYSTEM TRANSFORMATION WILL BE DONE AUTOMATICALLY ON
051465,000108:                                                                                          	# MULTIPLE TIMESTEP ENCKE INTEGRATION ONLY.  THUS IT IS POSSIBLE TO HAVE OUTPUT FROM SUCCESSIVE INTEGRATIONS IN
051466,000109:                                                                                          	# DIFFERENT SCALING.
051467,000110:                                                                                          	# HOWEVER, RATT, VATT WILL ALWAYS BE SCALED THE SAME.
051468,000111: 
051469,000112:                                                                                          	# 3.0 INPUT/OUTPUT
051470,000113:                                                                                          	# ----------------
051471,000114: 
051472,000115:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM INPUTS ARE THE FLAGS DESCRIBED IN APPENDIX A AND THE PERMANENT STATE VECTOR QUANTITIES DESCRIBED IN AP-
051473,000116:                                                                                          	# PENDIX B OF THE USERS GUIDE, PLUS THE DESIRED TIME TO INTEGRATE TO IN TDEC1 (A PUSH LIST LOCATION).
051474,000117:                                                                                          	# FOR INTEGRVS, THE RCV,VCV,TET OF THE TEMPORARY STATE VECTOR MUST BE SET, PLUS MOONFLAG AND MIDFLAG
051475,000118: 
051476,000119:                                                                                          	# FOR SIMULATION THE FOLLOWING QUANTITIES MUST BE PRESET ---
051477,000120:                                                                                          	#                                                                               EARTH   MOON
051478,000121:                                                                                          	#                                                                                29      27
051479,000122:                                                                                          	#       RRECTCSM(LEM)   -       RECTIFIED POSITION VECTOR       METERS          2       2
051480,000123: 
051481,000124:                                                                                          	#                                                                                7       5
051482,000125:                                                                                          	#       VRECTCSM(LEM)   -       RECTIFIED VELOCITY VECTOR       M/CSEC          2       2
051483,000126: 
051484,000127:                                                                                          	#                                                                                28      28
051485,000128:                                                                                          	#       TETCSM(LEM)     -       TIME STATE VECTOR IS VALID      CSEC            2       2
051486,000129:                                                                                          	#                               CUSTOMARILY 0, BUT NOTE LUNAR
051487,000130:                                                                                          	#                               ORBIT DEPENDENCE ON REAL TIME.
051488,000131: 
051489,000132:                                                                                          	#                                                                                22      18
051490,000133:                                                                                          	#       DELTAVCSM(LEM)  -       POSITION DEVIATION              METERS          2       2
051491,000134:                                                                                          	#                               0 IF TCCSM(LEM) = 0
051492,000135: 
051493,000136:                                                                                          	#                                                                                3       -1
051494,000137:                                                                                          	#       NUVCSM(LEM)     -       VELOCITY DEVIATION              M/CSEC          2       2
051495,000138:                                                                                          	#                               0 IF TCCSM(LEM) = 0
051497,000140:                                                                                          	#                                                                                29      27
051498,000141:                                                                                          	#       RCVCSM(LEM)     -       CONIC POSITION                  METERS          2       2
051499,000142:                                                                                          	#                               EQUALS RRECTCSM(LEM) IF
051500,000143:                                                                                          	#                               TCCSM(LEM) = 0
051501,000144: 
051502,000145:                                                                                          	#                                                                                7       5
051503,000146:                                                                                          	#       VCVCSM(LEM)     -       CONIC VELOCITY                  M/CSEC          2       2
051504,000147:                                                                                          	#                               EQUALS VRECTCSM(LEM) IF
051505,000148:                                                                                          	#                               TCCSM(LEM) = 0
051506,000149: 
051507,000150:                                                                                          	#                                                                                28      28
051508,000151:                                                                                          	#       TCCSM(LEM)      -       TIME SINCE RECTIFICATION        CSECS           2       2
051509,000152:                                                                                          	#                               CUSTOMARILY 0
051510,000153: 
051511,000154:                                                                                          	#                                                                1/2             17      16
051512,000155:                                                                                          	#       XKEPCSM(LEM)    -       ROOT OF KEPLERS EQUATION        M               2       2
051513,000156:                                                                                          	#                               0 IF TCCSM(LEM) = 0
051514,000157: 
051515,000158:                                                                                          	#       CMOONFLG        -       PERMANENT FLAGS CORRESPONDING                   0       0
051516,000159:                                                                                          	#       CMIDFLAG                TO MOONFLAG AND MIDFLAG                         0,1     0,1
051517,000160:                                                                                          	#       LMOONFLG                C = CSM, L = LM                                 0       0
051518,000161:                                                                                          	#       LMIDFLG                                                                 0,1     0,1
051519,000162: 
051520,000163:                                                                                          	#       SURFFLAG        -       LUNAR SURFACE FLAG                              0,1     0,1
051521,000164: 
051522,000165:                                                                                          	# IN ADDITION, IF (L)CMIDFLAG IS SET, THE INITIAL INPUT VALUES FOR LUNAR
051523,000166:                                                                                          	# SOLAR EPHEMERIDES SUBROUTINE AND PLANETARY INERTIAL ORIENTATION SUB-
051524,000167:                                                                                          	# ROUTINE MUST BE PRESET.
051525,000168: 
051526,000169:                                                                                          	# OUTPUT
051527,000170:                                                                                          	#       AFTER EVERY CALL TO INTEGRATION
051528,000171:                                                                                          	#                                                                       EARTH   MOON
051529,000172:                                                                                          	#                                                                        29      29
051530,000173:                                                                                          	#       0D      RATT    POSITION                        METERS          2       2
051531,000174: 
051532,000175:                                                                                          	#                                                                        7       7
051533,000176:                                                                                          	#       6D      VATT    VELOCITY                        M/CSEC          2       2
051534,000177: 
051535,000178:                                                                                          	#                                                                        28      28
051536,000179:                                                                                          	#       12D     TAT     TIME                                            2       2
051537,000180: 
051538,000181:                                                                                          	#                                                                        29      27
051539,000182:                                                                                          	#       14D     RATT1   POSITION                        METERS          2       2
051540,000183: 
051541,000184:                                                                                          	#                                                                        7       5
051542,000185:                                                                                          	#       20D     VATT1   VELOCITY                        M/CSEC          2       2
051543,000186: 
051544,000187:                                                                                          	#                                                        3   2           36      30
051545,000188:                                                                                          	#       26D     MU(P)   MU                              M /CS           2       2
051546,000189: 
051547,000190:                                                                                          	#       X1              MUTABLE ENTRY                                   -2      -10D
051548,000191: 
051549,000192:                                                                                          	#       X2              COORDINT
051550,000193:                                                                                          	#       X2              COORDINATE SYSTEM ORIGEN                        0       2
051551,000194:                                                                                          	#                       (THIS, NOT MOONFLAG, SHOULD BE
051553,000196:                                                                                          	#                       USED TO DETERMINE ORIGIN.)
051554,000197: 
051555,000198:                                                                                          	# IN ADDITION TO THE ABOVE, THE PERMANENT STATE VECTOR IS UPDATED WHENEVER
051556,000199:                                                                                          	# STATEFLG WAS SET AND WHENEVER A W-MATRIX IS TO BE INTEGRATED.  THE PUSH
051557,000200:                                                                                          	# COUNTER IS SET TO 0 AND OVERFLOW IS CLEARED BEFORE RETURNING TO THE
051558,000201:                                                                                          	# CALLING PROGRAM.
051559,000202: 
051560,000203:                                                                                          	# 4.0 CALLING SEQUENCES AND SAMPLE CODE
051561,000204:                                                                                          	# -------------------------------------
051562,000205: 
051563,000206:                                                                                          	#       A) PRECISION ORBITAL INTEGRATION.  CSMPREC, LEMPREC ENTRANCES
051564,000207:                                                                                          	#               L-X     STORE TIME TO 95T5791T5 T 95 PUS L9ST (T4531)
051565,000208:                                                                                          	#               L       CALL
051566,000209:                                                                                          	#               L+1             CSMPREC (OR LEMPREC)
051567,000210:                                                                                          	#               L+2     RETURN
051568,000211:                                                                                          	#          INPUT                                                           28
051569,000212:                                                                                          	#               TDEC1 (PD 32D) TIME TO INTEGRATE TO...CENTISECONDS SCALED 2
051570,000213:                                                                                          	#          OUTPUT
051571,000214:                                                                                          	#               THE DATA LISTED IN SECTION 3.0 PLUS
051572,000215:                                                                                          	#               RQVV    POSITION VECTOR OF VEHICLE WITH RESPECT TO SECONDARY
051573,000216:                                                                                          	#               BODY... METERS B-29 ONLY IF MIDFLAG = DIMOFLAG = 1
051574,000217:                                                                                          	#       B) CONIC INTEGRATION.  CSMCONIC, LEMCONIC ENTRANCES
051575,000218:                                                                                          	#               L-X     STORE TIME IN PUSH LIST (TDEC1)
051576,000219:                                                                                          	#               L       CALL
051577,000220:                                                                                          	#               L+1             CSMCONIC (OR LEMCONIC)
051578,000221:                                                                                          	#          INPUT/OUTPUT
051579,000222:                                                                                          	#               SAME AS PRECISION INTEGRATION, EXCEPT RQVV NOT SET
051580,000223:                                                                                          	#       C) INTEGRATE GIVEN STATE VECTOR.  INTEGRVS ENTRANCE
051581,000224:                                                                                          	#               CALL
051582,000225:                                                                                          	#                               INTSTALL
051583,000226:                                                                                          	#               VLOAD
051584,000227:                                                                                          	#                               POSITION VECTOR
051585,000228:                                                                                          	#               STOVL           RCV
051586,000229:                                                                                          	#                               VELOCITY VECTOR
051587,000230:                                                                                          	#               STODL           VCV
051588,000231:                                                                                          	#                               TIME STATE VECTOR VALID
051589,000232:                                                                                          	#               STODL           TET
051590,000233:                                                                                          	#                               FINAL RADIUS
051591,000234:                                                                                          	#               STORE           RFINAL
051592,000235:                                                                                          	#               SET(CLEAR)      SET(CLEAR)
051593,000236:                                                                                          	#                               INTYPFLAG
051594,000237:                                                                                          	#                               MOONFLAG
051595,000238:                                                                                          	#               SET(CLEAR)      DLOAD
051596,000239:                                                                                          	#                               DESIRED TIME
051597,000240:                                                                                          	#               STCALL          TDEC1
051598,000241:                                                                                          	#                               INTEGRVS
051599,000242:                                                                                          	#         INPUT
051600,000243:                                                                                          	#               RCV     POSITION VECTOR                 METERS
051601,000244:                                                                                          	#               VCV     VELOCITY VECTOR                 M/CSEC
051602,000245:                                                                                          	#               TET     TIME OF STATE VECTOR (MAY = 0)  CSEC B-28
051604,000247:                                                                                          	#               TDEC1   TIME TO INTEGRATE TO            CSEC B-28 (PD 32D)
051605,000248:                                                                                          	#                       (MAY BE INCREMENT IF TET=0)
051606,000249:                                                                                          	#         OUTPUT
051607,000250:                                                                                          	#               SAME AS FOR PRECISION OR CONIC INTEGRATION,
051608,000251:                                                                                          	#               DEPENDING ON INTYPFLG.
051609,000252:                                                                                          	#       D) INTEGRATE STATE VECTOR.  INTGRV ENTRANCE
051610,000253:                                                                                          	#               L-X     STORE TIME IN PUSH LIST (TDEC1) (MAY BE DONE AFTER CALL TO INTSTALL)
051611,000254:                                                                                          	#               L-8     CALL
051612,000255:                                                                                          	#               L-7
051613,000256:                                                                                          	#               L-6     SET(CLEAR)      SET(CLEAR)
051614,000257:                                                                                          	#               L-5                     VINTFLAG        1=CSM, 0=LM
051615,000258:                                                                                          	#               L-4                     INTYPFLAG       1=CONIC, 0=PRECISION
051616,000259:                                                                                          	#               L-3     SET(CLEAR)      SET(CLEAR)
051617,000260:                                                                                          	#               L-2                     DIMOFLAG        1=W-MATRIX, 0=NO W-MATRIX
051618,000261:                                                                                          	#               L-1                     D6OR9FLG        1=9X9, 0=6X6
051619,000262:                                                                                          	#               L       SET             DLOAD
051620,000263:                                                                                          	#               L+1                     STATEFLG        DESIRE PERMANENT UPDATE
051621,000264:                                                                                          	#               L+2                     FINAL RAD.      OF STATE VECTOR
051622,000265:                                                                                          	#               L+3     STCALL          RFINAL
051623,000266:                                                                                          	#               L+4                     INTEGRV
051624,000267:                                                                                          	#               L       CALL                            NORMAL USE -- WILL UPDATE STATE
051625,000268:                                                                                          	#               L+1                     INTEGRV         VECTOR IF DIMOFLAG=1. (STATEFLG IS
051626,000269:                                                                                          	#               L+2     RETURN                          ALWAYS RESET IN INTEGRATION AFTER
051627,000270:                                                                                          	#                                                       IT IS USED.)
051628,000271:                                                                                          	#         INPUT
051629,000272:                                                                                          	#               TDEC1 (PD 32D) TIME TO INTEGRATE TO     CSEC B-28
051630,000273:                                                                                          	#         OUTPUT
051631,000274:                                                                                          	#               SAME AS FOR PRECISION OR CONIC INTEGRATION
051632,000275:                                                                                          	#         THE PROGRAM WILL SET MOONFLAG, MIDFLAG DEPENDING ON
051633,000276:                                                                                          	#         THE PERMANENT STATE VECTOR REPRESENTATION.
