057406,000019:                                                                                          	##              2017-03-15 RSB  Comment-text fixes identified in 5-way
057407,000020:                                                                                          	##                              side-by-side diff of Luminary 69/99/116/131/210.
057408,000021: 
057409,000022:                                                                                          	## This source code has been transcribed or otherwise adapted from
057410,000023:                                                                                          	## digitized images of a hardcopy from the MIT Museum.  The digitization
057411,000024:                                                                                          	## was performed by Paul Fjeld, and arranged for by Deborah Douglas of
057412,000025:                                                                                          	## the Museum.  Many thanks to both.  The images (with suitable reduction
057413,000026:                                                                                          	## in storage size and consequent reduction in image quality as well) are
057414,000027:                                                                                          	## available online at www.ibiblio.org/apollo.  If for some reason you
057415,000028:                                                                                          	## find that the images are illegible, contact me at info@sandroid.org
057416,000029:                                                                                          	## about getting access to the (much) higher-quality images which Paul
057417,000030:                                                                                          	## actually created.
057418,000031:                                                                                          	##
057419,000032:                                                                                          	## Notations on the hardcopy document read, in part:
057420,000033:                                                                                          	##
057421,000034:                                                                                          	##      Assemble revision 001 of AGC program LMY99 by NASA 2021112-61
057422,000035:                                                                                          	##      16:27 JULY 14, 1969 
057423,000036: 
057425,000038:                                                                                          	# DISPLAYS CAN BE CLASSIFIED INTO THE FOLLOWING CATEGORIES -
057426,000039:                                                                                          	#       1.  PRIORITY DISPLAYS - DISPLAYS WHICH TAKE PRIORITY OVER ALL OTHER DISPLAYS.  USUALLY THESE DISPLAYS ARE SENT
057427,000040:                                                                                          	#           OUT UNDER CRITICAL ALARM CONDITIONS.
057428,000041:                                                                                          	#       2.  EXTENDED VERB DISPLAYS - ALL EXTENDED VERBS AND MARK ROUTINES SHOULD USE EXTENDED VERB (MARK) DISPLAYS.
057429,000042:                                                                                          	#       3.  NORMAL DISPLAYS - ALL MISSION PROGRAM DISPLAYS WHICH INTERFACE WITH THE ASTRONAUT DURING THE NORMAL
057430,000043:                                                                                          	#           SEQUENCE OF EVENTS.
057431,000044:                                                                                          	#       4.  MISC. DISPLAYS - ALL DISPLAYS NOT HANDLED BY THE DISPLAY INTERFACE ROUTINES.  THESE INCLUDE SUCH DISPLAYS AS
057432,000045:                                                                                          	#           MM DISPLAYS AND SPECIAL PURPOSE DISPLAYS HANDLED BY PINBALL.
057433,000046:                                                                                          	#       5.  ASTRONAUT INITIATED DISPLAYS - ALL DISPLAYS INITIATED EXTERNALLY.
057434,000047: 
057435,000048:                                                                                          	# THE FOLLOWING TERMS ARE USED TO DESCRIBE THE STATUS OF DISPLAYS -
057436,000049:                                                                                          	#       1.  ACTIVE - THE DISPLAY WHICH IS (1) BEING DISPLAYED TO THE ASTRONAUT AND WAITING FOR A RESPONSE OR
057437,000050:                                                                                          	#           (2) WAITING FIRST IN LINE FOR THE ASTRONAUT TO FINISH USING THE DSKY OR (3) BEING DISPLAYED ON THE DSKY
057438,000051:                                                                                          	#           BUT NOT WAITING FOR A RESPONSE.
057439,000052:                                                                                          	#       2.  INACTIVE - A DISPLAY WHICH HAS (1) BEEN ACTIVE BUT WAS INTERRUPTED BY A DISPLAY OF HIGHER PRIORITY,
057440,000053:                                                                                          	#           (2) BEEN PUT INTO THE WAITING LIST AT TIME IT WAS REQUESTED DUE TO THE FACT A HIGHER PRIORITY DISPLAY
057441,000054:                                                                                          	#           WAS ALREADY GOING, (3) BEEN INTERRUPTED BY THE ASTRONAUT (CALLED A PINBRANCH CONDITION, SINCE THIS TYPE
057442,000055:                                                                                          	#           OF INACTIVE DISPLAY IS USUALLY REACTIVATED ONLY BY PINBALL) OR (4) A DISPLAY WHICH HAS FINISHED BUT STILL
057443,000056:                                                                                          	#           HAS INFO SAVED FOR RESTART PURPOSES.
057444,000057: 
057445,000058:                                                                                          	# DISPLAY PRIORITIES WORK AS FOLLOWS -
057446,000059:                                                                                          	#       INTERRUPTS -
057447,000060:                                                                                          	#               1.  THE ASTRONAUT CAN INTERRUPT ANY DISPLAY WITH AN EXTERNAL DISPLAY REQUEST.
057448,000061:                                                                                          	#               2.  INTERNAL DISPLAYS CAN NOT BE SENT OUT WHEN THE ASTRONAUT IS USING THE DSKY.
057449,000062:                                                                                          	#               3.  PRIORITY DISPLAYS INTERRUPT ALL OTHER TYPES OF INTERNAL DISPLAYS.  A PRIORITY DISPLAY INTERRUPTING ANOTHER
057450,000063:                                                                                          	#                   PRIORITY DISPLAY WILL CAUSE AN ABORT UNLESS BIT14 IS SET FOR THE LINUS ROUTINE.
057451,000064:                                                                                          	#               4.  A MARK DISPLAY INTERRUPTS ANY NORMAL DISPLAY.
057452,000065:                                                                                          	#               5.  A MARK THAT INTERRUPTS A MARK COMPLETELY REPLACES IT.
057453,000066: 
057454,000067:                                                                                          	#       ORDER OF WAITING DISPLAYS -
057455,000068:                                                                                          	#               1.  ASTRONAUT EXTERNAL USE
057456,000069:                                                                                          	#               2.  PRIORITY
057457,000070:                                                                                          	#               3.  INTERRUPTED MARK
057458,000071:                                                                                          	#               4.  INTERRUPTED NORMAL
057459,000072:                                                                                          	#               5.  MARK TO BE REQUESTED (SEE DESCRIPTION OF ENDMARK)
057460,000073:                                                                                          	#               6.  MARK WAITING
057461,000074:                                                                                          	#               7.  NORMAL WAITING
057462,000075: 
057464,000077:                                                                                          	# THE DISPLAY ROUTINES ARE INTENDED TO SERVE AS AN INTERFACE BETWEEN THE USER AND PINBALL.  THE
057465,000078:                                                                                          	# FOLLOWING STATEMENTS CAN BE MADE ABOUT NORMAL DISPLAYS AND PRIORITY DISPLAYS (A DESCRIPTION OF MARK ROUTINES
057466,000079:                                                                                          	# WILL FOLLOW LATER):
057467,000080:                                                                                          	#       1.  ALL ROUTINES THAT END IN R HAVE AN IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER.  FOR ALL FLASHING DISPLAYS THIS RETURN
057468,000081:                                                                                          	#           IS TO THE USERS CALL CADR +4.  FOR THE ONLY NON FLASHING IMMEDIATE RETURN DISPLAY (GODSPR) THIS RETURN
057469,000082:                                                                                          	#           IS TO THE USERS CALLING LOC +1.
057470,000083:                                                                                          	#       2.  ALL ROUTINES NOT ENDING IN R DO NOT DO AN IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER.
057471,000084:                                                                                          	#       3.  ALL ROUTINES THAT END IN R START A SEPARATE JOB (MAKEPLAY) WITH USERS JOB PRIORITY.
057472,000085:                                                                                          	#       4.  ALL ROUTINES NOT ENDING IN R BRANCH DIRECTLY TO MAKEPLAY WHICH MAKES THESE DISPLAYS A PART OF THE
057473,000086:                                                                                          	#           USERS JOB.
057474,000087:                                                                                          	#       5.  ALL DISPLAY ROUTINES ARE CALLED VIA BANKCALL.
057475,000088:                                                                                          	#       6.  TO RESTART A DISPLAY THE USER WILL GENERALLY USE A PHASE OF ONE WITH DESIRED RESTART GROUP (SEE
057476,000089:                                                                                          	#           DESCRIPTION OF RESTARTS).
057477,000090:                                                                                          	#       7.  ALL FLASHING DISPLAYS HAVE 3 RETURNS TO THE USER FROM ASTRONAUT RESPONSES.  A TERMINATE (V34) BRANCHES
057478,000091:                                                                                          	#           TO THE USERS CALL CADR +1.  A PROCEED (V33) BRANCHES TO THE USERS CALL CADR +2.  AN ENTER OR RECYCLE
057479,000092:                                                                                          	#           (V32) BRANCHES TO THE USERS CALL CADR +3.
057480,000093:                                                                                          	#       8.  ALL ROUTINES MUST BE USED UNDER EXECUTIVE CONTROL.
057481,000094: 
057482,000095:                                                                                          	# A DESCRIPTION OF EACH ROUTINE WITH AN EXAMPLE FOLLOWS:
057483,000096:                                                                                          	#       GODSP IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A.  NO RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER.
057484,000097:                                                                                          	#               1.  GODSP IS NOT RESTARTABLE
057485,000098:                                                                                          	#               2.  A VERB PASTE WITH GODSP ALWAYS TURNS ON THE FLASH.
057486,000099:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     VXXNYY
057487,000100:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057488,000101:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GODSP
057489,000102:                                                                                          	#                       VXXNYY  OCT     0XXYY
057490,000103:                                                                                          	#       GODSPR IS THE SAME AS GODSP ONLY RETURN IS TO THE USER.
057491,000104:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     VXXNYY
057492,000105:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057493,000106:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GODSPR
057494,000107:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             IMMEDIATE RETURN OF GODSPR
057495,000108:                                                                                          	#       GOFLASH DISPLAYS A FLASHING VERB NOUN WITH NO IMMEDIATE RETURN TO THE USER.  3 RETURNS ARE POSSIBLE FROM
057496,000109:                                                                                          	#       THE ASTRONAUT (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
057497,000110:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     VXXNYY          VXX NYY WILL BE A FLASHING VERB NOUN.
057498,000111:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057499,000112:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GOFLASH
057500,000113:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             TERMINATE RETURN
057501,000114:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             PROCEED RETURN
057502,000115:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             ENTER OR RECYCLE RETURN
057503,000116:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF1 IS ENTERED WITH DESIRED CHECKLIST VALUE IN A.  GOPERF1 WILL DISPLAY THIS VALUE IN R1 BY MEANS OF A
057505,000118:                                                                                          	#       V01 N25.  A FLASHING PLEASE PERFORM ON CHECKLIST (V50 N25) IS THEN DISPLAYED.  NO IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO
057506,000119:                                                                                          	#       USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
057507,000120:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF1 BLANKS REGISTERS R2 AND R3
057508,000121:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     OCTXX           CODE FOR CHECKLIST VALUE XX
057509,000122:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057510,000123:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GOPERF1
057511,000124:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             TERMINATE RETURN
057512,000125:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             PROCEED RETURN
057513,000126:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             ENTER RETURN
057514,000127:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF2 IS ENTERED WITH A VARIABLE NOUN AND V01 (V00 FOR N10 OR N11) IN A.  GOPERF2 WILL FIRST DISPLAY THE
057515,000128:                                                                                          	#       REQUESTED NOUN BY MEANS OF A V01NYY OR A V00NYY.  PLEASE PERFORM ON NOUN (V50 NYY) THEN BECOMES A FLASHING
057516,000129:                                                                                          	#       DISPLAY.  NO IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
057517,000130:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF2 DOES NOT BLANK ANY REGISTERS
057518,000131:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     VXXNYY          VARIABLE NOUN YY. XX=00 OR 01.
057519,000132:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057520,000133:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GOPERF2
057521,000134:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             TERMINATE RETURN
057522,000135:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             PROCEED RETURN
057523,000136:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             ENTER RETURN
057524,000137:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF3 IS USED FOR A PLEASE PERFORM ON A PROGRAM NUMBER.  THE DESIRED PROGRAM NO. IS ENTERED IN A.  GOPERF3
057525,000138:                                                                                          	#       DISPLAYS THE NO. BY MEANS OF A V06 N07 FOLLOWED BY A FLASHING V50 N07 FOR A PLEASE PERFORM.  NO IMMEDIATE RETURN
057526,000139:                                                                                          	#       IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
057527,000140:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF3 BLANKS REGISTERS R2 AND R3
057528,000141:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     DECXX           REQUEST PERFORM ON PXX
057529,000142:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057530,000143:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GOPERF3
057531,000144:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             TERMINATE RETURN
057532,000145:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             PROCEED RETURN
057533,000146:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             ENTER RETURN
057534,000147:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF4 IS USED FOR A PLEASE PERFORM ON AN OPTION.  THE DESIRED OPTION IS ENTERED IN A AND STORED IN OPTION1.
057535,000148:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF4 DISPLAYS R1 AND R2 BY MEANS OF A V04N06 FOLLOWED BY A FLASHING V50N06 FOR A PLEASE PERFORM.  NO
057536,000149:                                                                                          	#       IMMEDIATE RETURN IS MADE TO THE USER (SEE NO. 7 ABOVE).
057537,000150:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     OCTXX           REQUEST PERFORM ON OPTION XX
057538,000151:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057539,000152:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GOPERF4
057540,000153:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             TERMINATE RETURN
057541,000154:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             PROCEED RETURN
057542,000155:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             ENTER RETURN
057543,000156:                                                                                          	#       GOPERF4 BLANKS REGISTER R3
057545,000158:                                                                                          	#       GODSPRET IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A WITH A RETURN TO THE USER AFTER THE DISPLAY HAS BEEN SENT
057546,000159:                                                                                          	#       OUT.
057547,000160:                                                                                          	#                               CAF     VXXNYY
057548,000161:                                                                                          	#                               TC      BANKCALL
057549,000162:                                                                                          	#                               CADR    GODSPRET
057550,000163:                                                                                          	#                               ...     ...             RETURN TO USER
057551,000164:                                                                                          	#       REGODSP IS USED TO DISPLAY A VERB NOUN ARRIVING IN A.  REGODSP IS THE SAME AS GODSP ONLY REGODSP REPLACES ANY
