057820,000433: 
057821,000434:                                                                                          	# RESTARTING DISPLAYS --
057822,000435: 
057823,000436:                                                                                          	# RULES FOR THE DSKY OPERATOR --
057824,000437:                                                                                          	#       1.  PROCEED AND TERMINATE SERVE AS RESPONSES TO REQUESTS FOR OPERATOR RESPONSE (FLASHING V/N).  AS LONG
057825,000438:                                                                                          	#           AS THERE IS ANY REQUEST AWAITING OPERATOR RESPONSE, ANY USE OF PROCEED OR TERMINATE WILL SERVE AS
057826,000439:                                                                                          	#           RESPONSES TO THAT REQUEST.  CARE SHOULD BE EXERCISED IN ATTEMPTING TO KILL AN OPERATOR INITIATED MONITOR
057827,000440:                                                                                          	#           WITH PROCEED AND TERMINATE FOR THIS REASON.
057828,000441:                                                                                          	#       2.  THE ASTRONAUT MUST RESPOND TO A PRIORITY DISPLAY NO SOONER THAN 2 SECONDS FROM THE TIME THE
057829,000442:                                                                                          	#           PROGRAM SENT OUT THE REQUEST FOR OPERATOR RESPONSE (THE ASTRONAUT WOULD SEE THIS DISPLAY FOR LESS TIME
057830,000443:                                                                                          	#           DUE TO TIME IT TAKES TO GET DISPLAY SENT OUT.)  IF THE ASTRONAUT RESPONDS TOO SOON, THE PRIORITY DISPLAY
057831,000444:                                                                                          	#            IS SENT OUT AGAIN -- AND AGAIN UNTIL AN ACCUMULATED 2 SECS      FROM THE TIME THE FIRST PRIORITY DISPLAY
057832,000445:                                                                                          	#           OUT.  THE SAME 2 SEC. DELAY WILL OCCUR AT 163.84 SECS OR IN ANY MULTIPLE OF THAT TIME DUE TO PROGRAM
057833,000446:                                                                                          	#           CONSIDERATION.
057834,000447:                                                                                          	#       3.  KEY RELEASE BUTTON -
057835,000448:                                                                                          	#           A)  IF THE KEY RELEASE LIGHT IS ON, IT SIMPLY RELEASES THE KEYBOARD AND DISPLAY FOR INTERNAL USE.
057836,000449:                                                                                          	#           B)  IF THE KEY RELEASE LIGHT IS OFF, AND IF SOME REQUEST FOR OPERATOR RESPONSE (FLASHING V/N) IS STILL
057837,000450:                                                                                          	#               AWAITING RESPONSE THEN IT RE-ESTABLISHES THE DISPLAYS THAT ORIGINALLY REQUESTED RESPONSE.
057838,000451:                                                                                          	#           IF AN OPERATOR WANTS THEREFORE TO RE-ESTABLISH BUT CONDITION (A) IS ENCOUNTERED, A SECOND DEPRESSION OF
057839,000452:                                                                                          	#           KEY RELEASE BUTTON MAY BE NECESSARY.
057840,000453:                                                                                          	#       4.  IT IS IMPORTANT TO ANSWER ALL REQUESTS FOR OPERATOR RESPONSE.
057841,000454:                                                                                          	#       5.  IT IS ALWAYS GOOD PRACTICE TO TERMINATE AN EXTENDED VERB BEFORE ASKING FOR ANOTHER ONE OR THE SAME ONE
057842,000455:                                                                                          	#           OVER AGAIN.
057843,000456: 
057844,000457:                                                                                          	# SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS--
057846,000459:                                                                                          	#       1.  MPAC +2 SAVED ONLY IN MARK DISPLAYS
057847,000460:                                                                                          	#       2.  GODSP(R), REGODSP(R), GOMARK(R) ALWAYS TURN ON THE FLASH IF ENTERED WITH A PASTE VERB REQUEST.
057848,000461:                                                                                          	#       3.  ALL NORMAL DISPLAYS ARE RESTARTABLE EXCEPT GODSP(R), REGODSP(R)
057849,000462:                                                                                          	#       4.  ALL EXTENDED VERBS WITH DISPLAYS SHOULD START WITH A TC TESTXACT AND FINISH WITH A TC ENDEXT.
057850,000463:                                                                                          	#       5.  GODSP(R) AND REGODSP(R) MUST BE IN THE SAME EBANK AND SUPERBANK AS THE LAST NORMAL DISPLAY RESTARTED
057851,000464:                                                                                          	#           BY A .1 RESTART PHASE CHANGE.
057852,000465:                                                                                          	#       6.  IN ORDER TO SET UP A NON DISPLAY .1 RESTART POINT, THE USER MUST MAKE CERTAIN THAT RESTREG CONTAINS THE
057853,000466:                                                                                          	#           CORRECT PRIORITY AND SUPERBANK AND THAT EBANKTEM CONTAINS THE CO
057854,000467:                                                                                          	#       7.  IF CLEANDSP IS RESTARTED VIA A .1 PHASE CHANGE, CAF ZERO SHOULD BE EXECUTED BEFORE THE TC BANKCALL.
057855,000468: 
