064210,000032:                                                                                          	## Notations on the hardcopy document read, in part:
064211,000033:                                                                                          	##
064212,000034:                                                                                          	##      Assemble revision 001 of AGC program LMY99 by NASA 2021112-61
064213,000035:                                                                                          	##      16:27 JULY 14, 1969 
064214,000036: 
064216,000038:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM NAME:         1/ACCS
064217,000039:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM WRITTEN BY:   BOB COVELLI AND MIKE HOUSTON
064218,000040:                                                                                          	# LAST MODIFICATION:    FEB. 14, 1969 BY G. KALAN
064219,000041: 
064220,000042:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM DESCRIPTION:
064221,000043:                                                                                          	#       1/ACCS PROVIDES THE INTERFACE BETWEEN THE GUIDANCE PROGRAMS AND THE DIGITAL AUTOPILOT.  WHENEVER THERE IS A
064222,000044:                                                                                          	#       CHANGE IN THE MASS OF THE VEHICLE, IN THE DEADBAND SELECTED, IN THE VEHICLE CONFIGURATION (ASCENT-DESCENT-
064223,000045:                                                                                          	#       DOCKED), AND DURING A FRESH START OR A RESTART, 1/ACCS IS CALLED TO COMMUNICATE THE DATA CHANGES TO THE DAP.
064224,000046: 
064225,000047:                                                                                          	#       THE INPUTS TO 1/ACCS ARE MASS, ACCELERATION (ABDELV), DEADBAND (DB), OFFSET ACCELERATIONS (AOSQ AND AOSR),
064226,000048:                                                                                          	#       STAGE VERIFY BIT (CHAN30, BIT2), DOCKED BIT (DAPBOOLS, BIT13), DRIFT BIT (DAPBOOLS, BIT8), USEQRJTS (DAPBOOLS,
064227,000049:                                                                                          	#       BIT14), AND SURFACE FLAG (FLAGWRD8, BIT8), AND CH5MASK.
064228,000050: 
064229,000051:                                                                                          	#       1/ACCS COMPUTES THE JET ACCELERATIONS (1JACC, 1JACCQ, 1JACCR) AS FUNCTIONS OF MASS.  1JACCU AND 1JACCV ARE
064230,000052:                                                                                          	#       FORMED BY RESOLVING 1JACCQ NAD 1JACCR.  IN THE DESCENT CASE, THE DESCENT ENGINE MOMENT ARM (L, PVT-CG) IS ALSO
064231,000053:                                                                                          	#       COMPUTED AS A FUNCTION OF MASS.  THE RATE OF CHANGE OF ACCELERATION DUE TO ROTATION OF THE GIMBAL (ACCDOTQ,
064232,000054:                                                                                          	#       ACCDOTR) IS ALSO COMPUTED IN THE DESCENT CASE.
064233,000055: 
064234,000056:                                                                                          	#       AFTER THE ABOVE COMPUTATIONS, THE PROGRAM 1/ACCONT COMPUTES THE RECIPROCAL NET ACCELERATIONS ABOUT THE P, U,
064235,000057:                                                                                          	#       AND V AXES (2 JETS FOR P AXIS, BOTH 1 AND 2 JETS FOR U AND V AXES), AND THE RECIPROCAL COAST ACCELERATIONS ABOUT
064236,000058:                                                                                          	#       THE P, U, AND V AXES.  THE ACCELERATION FUNCTIONS (ACCFCTZ1 AND ACCFCTZ5) ARE ALSO COMPUTED FOR THESE AXES.  THE
064237,000059:                                                                                          	#       FIRE AND COAST DEADBANDS AND AXISDIST ARE COMPUTED FOR EACH AXIS.  FLAT AND ZONE3LIM, THE WIDTH AND HEIGHT OF THE
064238,000060:                                                                                          	#       MINIMUM IMPULSE ZONE, ARE COMPUTED.  1/ACCONT ALSO SETS ACCSWU AND ACCSWV, WHICH INDICATE WHEN 1 JET ACCELERATION
064239,000061:                                                                                          	#       IS NOT SUFFICIENT TO PRODUCE MINIMUM ACCELERATION.  AT THE COMPLETION OF 1/ACCS, THE ACCSOKAY BIT IS SET.
064240,000062: 
064241,000063:                                                                                          	# SUBBOUTINES CALLED:
064242,000064:                                                                                          	#       TIMEGMBL
064243,000065:                                                                                          	#       MAKECADR
064244,000066:                                                                                          	#       ROT45DEG
064245,000067: 
064246,000068:                                                                                          	# CALLING SEQUENCE:
064247,000069:                                                                                          	#               TC      BANKCALL        (1/ACCS MUST BE CALL BY BANKCALL
